WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.630
In Great Yarmouth, Norfolk, 42.9 million
pounds of wall works protect 2,115 properties.

2
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:14.370
In Lincolnshire, the Boston Barrier protects
more than 13,000 homes and businesses.

3
00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:17.650
Yet on other stretches,
there is no wall at all.

4
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.970
A house stands near the
edge of a crumbling cliff.

5
00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:23.770
England has 20 Shoreline Management Plans,

6
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:27.830
each planning a stretch of
coast as far ahead as 2105.

7
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.150
So why does England defend some stretches,

8
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.710
and let the sea take others?

9
00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:37.390
In this mission, you'll see how moving
sand links one beach to the next.

10
00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:41.950
Then you'll learn how forecasts, warnings
and risk maps help keep coastal people

11
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.130
safe.

12
00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:47.750
Your mission: explain why England defends
some stretches of coast and lets the

13
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:49.080
sea take others.
